@startuml
title Carte des contextes DDD - CanTelcoX Phase 1

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #64748B
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

rectangle "Clients & Identite\nsvc-clients-identite" as CI #DBEAFE
rectangle "Catalogue & Offres\nsvc-catalogue-offres" as CO #DBEAFE
rectangle "Commandes & Activations\nsvc-commandes-activations" as CA #DBEAFE
rectangle "Lignes & Services\nsvc-lignes-services" as LS #DBEAFE
rectangle "Usage / Rating /\nFacturation\nsvc-usage-facturation" as UF #DBEAFE
rectangle "Conformite & Audit\nsvc-conformite-audit" as AUD #FEF3C7

rectangle "KYC / scoring\nsimule Phase 1" as KYC
rectangle "OTP / MFA\nsimule Phase 1" as MFA
rectangle "Hub portabilite\nMSISDN simule" as PORT
rectangle "HLR / HSS / UDM\nfree5GC ou mock" as HLR
rectangle "Paiement\nsimule" as PAY
rectangle "CDR / Mediation\nsimules" as CDR

note right of AUD
Conformite & Audit recoit les
evenements critiques dans un
journal append-only.
end note

' Positioning helpers
CI -[hidden]down-> CA
CO -[hidden]up-> CA
CA -[hidden]right-> LS
LS -[hidden]right-> UF
UF -[hidden]down-> AUD

KYC -[hidden]down-> MFA
MFA -[hidden]down-> CI
PAY -[hidden]down-> CDR
CDR -[hidden]left-> UF
PORT -[hidden]down-> HLR
HLR -[hidden]left-> LS

' Clients & Identite
CI --> KYC : ACL\nverification identite
CI --> MFA : ACL\nOTP / MFA
CI --> CA : client, identite,\nscore risque
CI --> AUD : evenements identite\net MFA

' Catalogue & Offres
CO --> CA : offre, prix,\neligibilite
CO --> AUD : validation offre\nou version catalogue

' Commandes & Activations
CA --> LS : demande\nactivation
CA --> UF : commande,\nchangement forfait
CA --> AUD : evenements commande\net activation

' Lignes & Services
LS --> CA : ligne active,\nMSISDN, forfait
LS --> PORT : ACL\nportabilite
LS --> HLR : ACL\nactivation reseau
LS --> AUD : evenements ligne

' Usage / Rating / Facturation
UF --> PAY : ACL\npaiement facture
UF --> CDR : ACL\nusages CDR
UF --> AUD : evenements facture\net paiement

note bottom
Les systemes externes simules sont isoles par des ACL/adapters afin
de proteger le modele de domaine interne des contrats techniques externes.
end note

@enduml
